# Interaction performance (priority)

TestiGo screens are data-dense (checklists, defects, PRs). **Treat click/keystroke lag as a bug.** Optimize before shipping list UIs, mark buttons, and TipTap dialogs.

Reference fix: checklist page (`DocumentChecklistViewer`, `CaseTable`) and `docs/qa/checklist-marking.test-cases.md`.

## Hard rules

1. **One layout tree** — Do not mount mobile *and* desktop variants and hide one with `lg:hidden` / `hidden lg:block`. CSS hide still runs React work. Use `useMediaQuery` (`~/hooks/useMediaQuery`, Tailwind `lg` = `(min-width: 64rem)`) when the breakpoint changes *what* is rendered.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — both trees reconcile on every mark click
<>
  <div className="lg:hidden">{rows.map(...)}</div>
  <div className="hidden lg:block"><DesktopTable rows={rows} /></div>
</>

// ✅ GOOD
const isDesktop = useMediaQuery("(min-width: 64rem)");
return isDesktop ? <DesktopTable rows={rows} /> : <StackedList rows={rows} />;
```

2. **Keep hot paths cheap** — Collapsed/list previews must not run `ReactMarkdown` or TipTap. Use plain text (`plainTextFromMarkdown` / truncate). Parse once and cache (`getCaseBodySections`), not per row per click.

3. **Isolate expensive editors** — TipTap/`MarkdownEditor` drafts stay **inside** the dialog or expanded row. Do not lift every keystroke into a parent that owns the full case list. Mount card feedback editors only when opened, not N editors at once.

4. **Stabilize list updates** — Batch related state (e.g. mark + `"pending"` save) in one event so one click ≠ two full-list commits. `useMemo` row data; `memo` rows with **data** equality (`mark`, `saveState`, ids) so changing one row does not re-render every row. Prefer a shared `EMPTY_MARK` constant over `?? { status: null, feedback: "" }` each render.

5. **Precompute permissions** — Build a `Map<caseId, { canMark, reason }>` once; do not rescan assignments inside every row mapper on each click.

## Done check

- [ ] A mark/filter click on a 20+ row list does not hitch the toolbar
- [ ] Typing in Add/Edit dialogs does not re-render the list behind the overlay
- [ ] Only one responsive layout is mounted
- [ ] No `ReactMarkdown` / TipTap on the collapsed scan path
